# Mandalon
SvelteKit remake of [mandalon.se](https://mandalon.se). B2B site for chip packaging, bonding, and consulting services.
## Stack
- **Svelte 5** with runes mode forced project-wide (`$props()`, `$derived()`, `{@render children()}`)
- **SvelteKit 2** with **Vite 5**
- **Node 18.20.8** (see `.nvmrc`)
- **Adapter:** `@sveltejs/adapter-node` (README also mentions static deploy to `build/` but this is obsolete information and should be updated in the future)
- **JS + JSDoc** with `checkJs: true` — TypeScript used selectively (`lang="ts"` in some components)
- **Lint/format:** ESLint + Prettier (`npm run lint`, `npm run format`)
- **Type check:** `npm run check` (svelte-check)
- **Line endings:** LF only (Unix newlines) — enforced via `.gitattributes` (`* text=auto eol=lf`). Do not use CRLF (carriage return). New and edited files must end lines with `\n` only.
## Commands
```bash
npm install
npm run dev      # local development
npm run build    # production build
npm run check    # svelte-check
npm run lint     # prettier + eslint
```
## i18n

- Routes live under `src/routes/[[lang]]/` — Swedish is default (`/paketering`), English uses `/en/…` (`/en/packaging`)
- Copy is keyed by locale in `src/lib/content/site.js` (`siteContent`); `+layout.js` passes it to pages as `data.content`
- Canonical pages use Swedish slugs; EN routes are thin wrappers that import the SV page (see `svelte-components.mdc`)

## Conventions

- **Copy:** User-facing text lives in `src/lib/content/site.js` — pages consume it as `data.content`; components receive copy via props (never hardcoded)
- **Code comments:** Swedish or English
- **Reference page:** `paketering/+page.svelte` — target structure for migrated pages
- **Active refactor:** component/style consolidation — see `refactoring.mdc`